From: Sobs <antohasobne@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mainui: over a game the menu opens on Resume; Start closes it, Back quick loads

The main menu over a game had no item chosen: A did nothing, Start (a
handheld's F1, which opened it) did not close it and Up went round to
Quit. Now Resume Game is chosen when it opens over a game, Start closes
it as on a console, and Back (the handheld's F2, the quick load in the
game) loads the quick save from the menu too, also before a game, in the
main menu of a game just started.

--- a/3rdparty/mainui/menus/Main.cpp
+++ b/3rdparty/mainui/menus/Main.cpp
@@ -44,6 +44,7 @@
 	CMenuMain() : CMenuFramework( "CMenuMain" ) { }
 
 	bool KeyDown( int key ) override;
+	void Show() override;
 
 	void QuitDialogCb();
 
@@ -126,6 +127,19 @@
 */
 bool CMenuMain::KeyDown( int key )
 {
+	// a gamepad's Start (a handheld's F1) opened the menu over the game and
+	// closes it again, as on a console; Back (F2) is the quick load there,
+	// before a game too (the main menu of a game just started)
+	if( key == K_START_BUTTON && CL_IsActive() && !dialog.IsVisible() )
+	{
+		UI_CloseMenu();
+		return true;
+	}
+	if( key == K_BACK_BUTTON && !dialog.IsVisible() )
+	{
+		EngFuncs::ClientCmd( false, "loadquick\n" );
+		return true;
+	}
 	if( UI::Key::IsEscape( key ) )
 	{
 		if ( CL_IsActive( ))
@@ -143,6 +157,21 @@
 }
 
 /*
+=================
+CMenuMain::Show
+
+Over a game: Resume Game chosen, so A goes back to it (the cursor was on
+nothing: A did nothing, and Up went round to Quit)
+=================
+*/
+void CMenuMain::Show()
+{
+	CMenuFramework::Show();
+	if( CL_IsActive() && resumeGame.IsVisible() )
+		SetCursorToItem( resumeGame );
+}
+
